# Variables from http-client.env.json and http-client.private.env.json beside this file. Pick "dev" in the
# response view's environment dropdown first (http.selectEnvironment); try "prod" too, and "local", which
# only the private file defines. Requests go to httpbin.org's /anything, which echoes back what it got, so
# the response shows what each {{variable}} became.

@who = {{users[0].name}}

### Values from the selected environment, the private file, and $shared
# "token" comes from the private file, which wins over the public one.
GET {{host}}/anything?title={{title}}&who={{who}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Api-Version: {{api.version}}
X-Greeting: {{greeting}}

### Nested objects with dots, arrays with indexes
POST {{host}}{{api.paths.echo}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first": "{{users[0].name}} ({{users[0].role}})",
  "second": "{{users[1].name}} ({{users[1].role}})"
}

### A later @who line takes over for the requests below it
# An @name = value line goes at the top of a request's section: after a body, it would be part of the body.
@who = {{users[1].name}}
GET {{host}}/anything?who={{who}}

### A typo is underlined as you type; sent anyway, it goes out empty and is listed in the warnings
GET {{host}}/anything?title={{tittle}}
